cff-version: 1.2.0
title: GeoSpaX
message: "If you use GeoSpaX, please cite it. GeoSpaX is built on GeoLibre — cite both if you use the platform. Metadata from this file powers GitHub's 'Cite this repository' button."
type: software
abstract: "GeoSpaX 2.0.0 — Multi-domain geospatial analysis GIS built on GeoLibre 3.0.0. A specialised fork of opengeos/GeoLibre for applied environmental and geospatial analysis (FR422 habitat-assessment workflow, PNG University of Technology lineage jm0535/map-kit v1.4.3 → GeoSpaX v2.0.0 platform rewrite). Adds twelve bundled GSX domain workbenches (Agriculture, Biodiversity, Climate, Conservation, Disaster, Environment, Forestry, Geoscience, Hydrology, LULC, Marine, Soil), each with a built-in How-to-Cite section and user guide, @geospax/analysis v2.0.0 (18 dependency-light modules: protection gap, WLC suitability, fragmentation/connectivity, SDM BIOCLIM/Mahalanobis, change, hydrology, diversity indices, Jenks, SCP HiGHS-WASM) and @geospax/data v2.0.0 (GBIF/OBIS/iNat/WoRMS/WorldBank + GEBCO/ecoregion/forest/marine/SPREP, citation-carried), while retaining GeoLibre's 1,000+ WebAssembly geoprocessing tools, Tauri desktop/mobile, and Jupyter."
